    "B": "a > b and p < q",
    "C": "a < b and p < q",
    "D": "a < b and p > q",
    "Answer": "a < b and p > q",
    "Image": "",
    "Explaination": "For a lead network the zero is nearer to the origin than the pole, so a < b. For a lag network the pole is nearer to the origin than the zero, so q < p, i.e. p > q."
